From 8465a0cf8a676a98e214febe581ba499440f6e53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valentin Haudiquet <valentin.haudiquet@canonical.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 00:51:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] board: mediatek: mt8183: hand Linux the mtu3 view of SSUSB
 from bootcmd

The krane DT describes the single SSUSB block twice: the mtu3 wrapper
(/soc/usb@11201000 -- the Linux view, whose parent owns the shared
IPPC register block) and its xHCI child (/soc/usb@11201000/
usb@11200000), which carries an extra "ippc" reg entry so U-Boot's
xhci-mtk driver finds the IPPC it needs.  The two shapes cannot
coexist in the kernel: with the child keeping its ippc reg, the
kernel's xhci-mtk on the child deterministically fails to request the
region the mtu3 parent already claimed (-EBUSY) and USB never comes
up; without mtu3 claiming it, the two drivers instead race for it at
probe, making USB work per boot.

Fix the handoff instead.  From bootcmd -- after preboot's usb start,
where U-Boot has finished probing (its xhci-mtk needs the child's
ippc), so the property changes, which splice the FDT structure block,
are safe:

  - echo marker: prints the bootcmd version on every boot, so a stale
    payload on the boot media is visible at a glance.
  - fdt set ... compatible mediatek,mt8183-mtu3 mediatek,mtu3: the
    parent node is also "simple-mfd", and without removing that
    string the kernel populates the child xHCI device at boot.
    Whenever its driver binds before mtu3 probed, the child starts
    with has_ippc=false against an unpowered host IP -- "USB0 root
    hub has no ports", all USB dead for the boot, no retry.
    (mtu3's own probe can defer and retry, so module load order in
    the initramfs cannot fix this race.)  Note this must be a value
    rewrite, not "fdt rm": simple-mfd is a string inside
    "compatible", not a property.
  - fdt set ... reg/reg-names: reshape the child to mac-only, and
    fdt rm ... phys: drop the T-PHY list the -u-boot.dtsi overlay put
    on the child for U-Boot's own xhci-mtk.  Upstream the phys belong
    to the mtu3 parent; left on the child, the kernel's xhci-mtk gets
    the same two PHYs a second time and init/powers them behind the
    parent's back.  phy_init() and phy_power_on() are refcounted so
    this is benign today, but it is not the shape the kernel expects
    and it makes the child's teardown asymmetric with the parent's.

When the kernel's mtu3 later probes, ssusb_host_setup powers the host
IP and of_platform_populate creates the child at that point; it binds
the already-loaded xhci driver immediately, with the ports the parent
enabled.  bootefi then hands exactly this blob to the kernel as its
device tree, and U-Boot keeps using its own xHCI as before (the parent
still matches the mtu3 driver without the simple-mfd string).

The edit lives in krane.env rather than C on purpose: last_stage_init
runs BEFORE preboot, where the same splices would corrupt the tree of
the not-yet-probed USB stack.
---
 board/mediatek/mt8183/krane.env | 36 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 36 insertions(+)

diff --git a/board/mediatek/mt8183/krane.env b/board/mediatek/mt8183/krane.env
index e9e8bd4ecbe..73d5c1bf3a6 100644
--- a/board/mediatek/mt8183/krane.env
+++ b/board/mediatek/mt8183/krane.env
@@ -1,3 +1,39 @@
 stdin=serial,usbkbd
 stdout=serial,vidconsole
 stderr=serial,vidconsole
+
+/*
+ * The single SSUSB block is described twice: the mtu3 wrapper
+ * (/soc/usb@11201000, the Linux view: the parent owns the shared IPPC
+ * block) and its xHCI child (/soc/usb@11201000/usb@11200000, which
+ * carries an extra ippc reg entry for U-Boot's xhci-mtk driver).  When
+ * Linux sees the child WITH ippc, its xhci-mtk deterministically fails
+ * to request the region the mtu3 parent already owns -> no host
+ * controller -> no USB.
+ *
+ * Hand Linux the upstream shape instead, and make the bring-up
+ * self-serializing:
+ *
+ *   - rewrite the parent's "compatible" without its "simple-mfd"
+ *     string: with it, the kernel populates the child xHCI device at
+ *     boot, and whenever its driver binds before mtu3 probed, the
+ *     child starts with has_ippc=false against an unpowered host IP --
+ *     "USB0 root hub has no ports", all USB dead for the boot, no
+ *     retry.
+ *   - reshape the child to mac-only ("ippc" reg entry removed), and
+ *     drop the "phys" list the overlay added for U-Boot's xhci-mtk:
+ *     upstream the T-PHYs hang off the mtu3 parent, and leaving them
+ *     on the child has the kernel's xhci-mtk init and power the very
+ *     PHYs the parent already brought up.
+ *
+ * All three edits run from bootcmd, i.e. AFTER preboot's "usb start":
+ * U-Boot has finished probing by then (its xhci-mtk needs the child's
+ * ippc), so the property changes -- which splice the FDT structure
+ * block -- are safe here.  When the kernel's mtu3 later probes,
+ * ssusb_host_setup powers the host IP and of_platform_populate creates
+ * the child at that point; it binds the already-loaded xhci driver
+ * immediately, with the ports the parent enabled.  bootefi then hands
+ * exactly this blob to the kernel.  (The parent still matches the
+ * mtu3 driver without the simple-mfd string.)
+ */
+bootcmd=echo krane-bootcmd-v4 && fdt addr ${fdtcontroladdr} && fdt set /soc/usb@11201000 compatible mediatek,mt8183-mtu3 mediatek,mtu3 && fdt set /soc/usb@11201000/usb@11200000 reg '<0x0 0x11200000 0x0 0x1000>' && fdt set /soc/usb@11201000/usb@11200000 reg-names mac && fdt rm /soc/usb@11201000/usb@11200000 phys && bootefi bootmgr
-- 
2.53.0

